          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_pcXW9Y": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is the difference between Xinzuo knife series?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_7EtcXB": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Xinzuo groups its kitchen knives into four core series, each designed for a different budget and performance level:</p><p><strong>Supreme Series</strong> — dependable everyday knives with strong edge retention for home cooks upgrading from supermarket blades.</p><p><strong>Retro Series</strong> — a step up in steel and finish, holding a sharper edge for longer between honing sessions.</p><p><strong>Mo Series</strong> — high-performance blades with genuine Damascus cladding and a distinctive layered pattern.</p><p><strong>LAN Series</strong> — our flagship range, built with premium steels and refined balance for serious cooks and professional kitchens.</p><p>Compare series on our <a href=\"/pages/series-comparison\">series comparison page</a> or shop by type in <a href=\"/collections/all-products\">all products</a>.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_7EtcXB"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_6tQbnh": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Is the Damascus pattern on Mo and LAN series knives real?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_g7yrea": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Yes. On Mo and LAN series knives, the Damascus appearance comes from layered steel forged around a high-performance core—not a surface print or laser etch.</p><p>Multiple steel layers are folded and clad to create the wave pattern you see on the blade. This construction is part of the knife's structure and can also help reduce sticking when slicing proteins and vegetables.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_g7yrea"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_BCTefQ": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_dash_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Can Xinzuo kitchen knives go in the dishwasher?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_4yTDmM": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>We do not recommend putting Xinzuo knives in the dishwasher. High heat, moisture, and harsh detergents can dull the edge, damage handles, and may affect warranty coverage.</p><p>For best results, hand-wash with mild soap, dry immediately, and store in a knife block, sheath, or magnetic holder. This routine protects sharpness and extends the life of your blade.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_4yTDmM"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_wRmVEU": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_dash_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Where are Xinzuo kitchen knives made?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_HxKVBr": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Xinzuo knives are manufactured in Yangjiang, China—widely known as the knife-making capital of the world, with a craft heritage spanning more than 1,400 years.</p><p>We work with specialist forges and heat-treatment partners there, then sell direct to Australian customers. That model lets us use premium steels and construction at a fair price, without the markups typical of legacy retail brands.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "color": "var(--color-foreground)",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_HxKVBr"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_4Tg8BV": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_dash_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What warranty and returns does Xinzuo Australia offer?",
                "content": "",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_e7gcyQ": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Eligible orders include a <strong>30-day change-of-mind return</strong> window, plus a <strong>lifetime warranty</strong> against manufacturing defects (such as blade or handle faults from production).</p><p>Normal wear, misuse, and damage from improper care (including dishwasher use) are not covered. Your purchase is also protected under <strong>Australian Consumer Law</strong>.</p><p>For returns, warranty, or order help, contact us at <a href=\"mailto:support@xinzuo.com.au\">support@xinzuo.com.au</a> or visit our <a href=\"/pages/warranty\">warranty page</a>.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "normal",
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
